SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT AND MUTUAL RELEASE

 This Settlement Agreement and Mutual Release (the “Agreement”), dated January ___, 2001,  is entered into and executed by and between Enron Power Marketing, Inc. (“EPMI”), and Tennessee Valley Authority ("TVA”) (EPMI and TVA are referred to herein collectively as "the Parties").

RECITALS

 1. WHEREAS the Parties have executed and entered into a Master Option Purchase Agreement dated December 6, 1995 (“MOPA”); and

 2. WHEREAS, a dispute has arisen among the Parties in the case styled Civil Action No. 1:99 - CV-262; Enron Power Marketing, Inc. v. Tennessee Valley Authority; In the United States District Court for the Eastern District of Tennessee at Chattanooga (the "Litigation"); and

 3. WHEREAS, the Parties have agreed to compromise and settle their disputes, and as part of that agreement have agreed to enter into this Settlement Agreement and Mutual Release;

 NOW THEREFORE, for good and valuable consideration the Parties do hereby agree as follows:

AGREEMENTS AND RELEASES

 4. For and in consideration of the releases and agreements set out in this Agreement, EPMI agrees to pay to TVA the sum of TWO HUNDRED AND FORTY-FOUR MILLION and 00/100 DOLLARS ($244,000,000.00) ("the Settlement Sum").  Payment of the Settlement Sum shall be made by wire transfer on or before January 15, 2001 according to the following wire transfer instructions:
_________________________

_________________________

 5. For and in consideration of the releases and agreements set out in this Agreement, the Parties agree that the MOPA is hereby terminated in its entirety and is without further force and effect.  It is agreed that all rights, duties, and obligations of parties arising out of the MOPA are fully and finally discharged by this Agreement.

 6.  For and in consideration of the releases and agreements set out in this Agreement TVA hereby releases and forever discharges EPMI, together with each of EPMI’s parent corporations, affiliates, subsidiaries, and previous and present officers, directors, representatives, accountants, shareholders, members, agents, employees, and attorneys, from any and all claims, demands, liabilities, responsibilities, and causes of action, legal or equitable, in contract or in tort, whether known or unknown, existing as of the date of this agreement, based upon, arising from, or relating in any way to the MOPA or the claims and counterclaims asserted or any of the matters at issue in the Litigation.

 7. For and in consideration of the releases and agreements set out in this Agreement EPMI hereby releases and forever discharges TVA, together with each of TVA’s affiliates, subsidiaries, and previous and present officers, directors, representatives, accountants, shareholders, members, agents, employees, and attorneys, from any and all claims, demands, liabilities, responsibilities, and causes of action, legal or equitable, in contract or in tort, whether known or unknown, existing as of the date of this agreement, based upon, arising from, or relating in any way to the MOPA or the claims and counterclaims asserted or any of the matters at issue in the Litigation.

. 8. The Parties agree that they shall jointly file a stipulation of dismissal, with prejudice, of all claims, counterclaims,  and causes of action asserted by them in the Litigation within ten days after: i) both Parties have executed this Agreement; and ii) EPMI has paid the Settlement Sum to TVA. 

 9. This Agreement contains the entire understanding and agreement of the Parties, and supersedes all other written or oral exchanges, arrangements, or negotiations between them or their representatives and may not be altered, amended, or modified, except by a writing properly executed by the party to be charged thereby.  Each of the Parties hereby represents and warrants that in entering into this Agreement it is not relying on any representation, warranty, or agreement not expressly set forth in this Agreement.

 10. This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Texas.

 11. This Settlement Agreement and Mutual Release may be executed in multiple counterparts, each of which shall be deemed to be and have the same force and effect as an original, and all of which, taken together, shall constitute and be construed as a single agreement.

 12. Each of the signatories to this Agreement represent that they have read it, have consulted with counsel regarding its terms, and that each is duly authorized to execute this Settlement Agreement and Mutual Release on their own behalf or on behalf of the party that they represent.

 13. The parties agree that they will not disclose this Agreement, or any matter relating thereto or to the underlying dispute to any third party without the prior consent of the other party; provided however, that nothing in this Settlement Agreement and Mutual Release shall limit or prohibit the ability of any Party, without the knowledge or consent of any other Party, to make legally required disclosure in response to regulatory or financial inquiries, subpoenas, or to discharge any disclosure obligations they may have under any applicable federal or state laws, or to disclose the terms of this Settlement Agreement and Mutual Release to any regulatory agency having jurisdiction over one or more of the Parties.

